    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1` (the `POST /api/owners` handler), which is where all the owner-create business rules live.\n\n**Changes to `src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:**\n\n1. **Injected `HttpServletRequest`** via the constructor so the handler can read the `Idempotency-Key` header (the generated `OwnersApi.addOwner(...)` signature is fixed and can't take a header param).\n\n2. **Added a key\u2192id store** (`ConcurrentHashMap<String, Integer> idempotentOwnerIds`) mapping each seen idempotency key to the id of the owner created under it.\n\n3. **In `addOwner`:**\n   - At the start, if an `Idempotency-Key` header is present and already recorded, look up the original owner and return it with **200 OK** \u2014 short-circuiting before any validation or duplicate checks, so the repeat neither creates a duplicate nor 409s.\n   - After a successful `saveOwner`, record the new owner's id under the key.\n\n4. **Added an `idempotencyKey()` helper** that returns the trimmed header value, or `null` when absent/blank (treated uniformly as \"no key\").\n\n**Behavior:** A first create with a key returns 201 CREATED as before; a repeat with the same key returns the originally created owner with 200 OK. Requests without the header are unaffected. The acceptance test `coreIdempotentRepeat` passes (the second POST takes the idempotent path \u2014 confirmed by only one \"Owner created\" audit line), and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
