    "probe_text": "POST `/api/owners` is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:187`), the implementation of the generated `OwnersApi.addOwner` (mapped `POST /owners` under the `/api` base). Here is everything that happens, in order. I've tagged each step as **[V]** validation (can reject the request) or **[S]** side-effect (mutates the owner, persists, logs, etc.).\n\n## Before the method body runs (Spring MVC)\n\n1. **[V] Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role.\n2. **[V] Bean validation of the request body** \u2014 `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (`OwnersApi.java:86`). Constraints on the DTO:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine1` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email`\n   - `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 `@Valid` (parsed as ISO dates)\n   - `title`, `postcode`, `sharesHousehold` \u2014 no constraints\n\n## Inside `addOwner`, in execution order\n\n3. **[S] Idempotency replay check** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header (`idempotencyKey()`). If the key was seen before **and** that owner still exists, the original owner is returned as `200 OK` and everything below is skipped (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:188-197`).\n4. **[V] Required-field guard** (`validateRequiredOwnerFields`) \u2014 rejects with `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (400) if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (neither `addressLine1` nor flat `address` is non-blank after normalization), `city`, or `telephone` is blank. This catches present-but-blank values that bean validation misses.\n5. **[S] Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`), with `id` and `pets` ignored.\n6. **[V]+[S] Telephone normalization** (`normalizeTelephone`, then `setTelephone`) \u2014 strips spaces/dashes/brackets, keeps a leading `+`/country code or assumes `+61` and drops a leading `0`; **rejects** (400) if the result isn't `+` followed by 8\u201315 digits, or if the national-number length is wrong for a known country code (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Stores the normalized E.164 value.\n7. **[V]+[S] Email normalization** (`normalizeEmail`, then `setEmail`) \u2014 `null` is allowed; otherwise **rejects** (400) if it fails `EMAIL_PATTERN` or its domain is in the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Stores the trimmed, lower-cased value.\n8. **[S] Address normalization** (`applyAddress`) \u2014 prefers structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (upper-cased, whitespace collapsed, `ST/RD/AVE` expanded) and composes the flat `address`; otherwise normalizes the flat `address` and clears the structured lines.\n9. **[V] Postcode validation** (`validatePostcode`) \u2014 `null` allowed; otherwise **rejects** (400) if not 4 digits, or if out of the city's region range (Sydney/NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne/VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane/QLD 4000\u20134099). Unknown cities accept any 4-digit value.\n10. **[V] Future registration date** (`rejectFutureRegistrationDate`) \u2014 checks the **supplied** date (before roll-forward); **rejects** with `FutureRegistrationDateException` if it is after today.\n11. **[S] Default registration date** \u2014 if none supplied, defaults to `LocalDate.now()`.\n12. **[S] Roll to business day** (`rollToBusinessDay`, then `setRegistrationDate`) \u2014 advances the date past weekends and the fixed 2026 public-holiday list to the next business day. This adjusted date feeds every later date-derived value.\n13. **[V] Daily create limit** (`rejectDailyLimitReached`) \u2014 **rejects** with `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` if \u2265 100 owners already share the (adjusted) registration date.\n14. **[V] City capacity** (`rejectCityAtCapacity`) \u2014 **rejects** with `OwnerCityCapacityExceededException` if the city (compared case/whitespace-insensitively) already has \u2265 50 owners.\n15. **[S] Household id** (`setHouseholdId(householdId(...))`) \u2014 deterministic SHA-256-based id over normalized `lastName` + `postcode`.\n16. **[V] Duplicate-household check** (`rejectDuplicateIdentity`) \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold` is true, **rejects** with `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (409) if any non-deleted owner already has the same `householdId`.\n17. **[S] Possible-duplicate flags** (`assignPossibleDuplicate`) \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold`, sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` to the earliest non-deleted owner with the same last name + postcode but a *different* phone.\n18. **[S] Namesake count** (`setNamesakeCount(countNamesakes(...))`) \u2014 number of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n19. **[S] Bulk-signup warning** (`setBulkSignupWarning(isBulkSignupDay(...))`) \u2014 true if > 80 owners already share the registration date.\n20. **[S] Household size** (`setHouseholdSize(countHousehold(...))`) \u2014 count of owners in the household, including this one.\n21. **[S] Customer code** (`setCustomerCode(buildCustomerCode(...))`) \u2014 `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city, hash of phone+lastName), de-duplicated by appending `-<n>` on collision.\n22. **[S] Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`, which assigns the id.\n23. **[S] Record idempotency key** \u2014 if a key was supplied, stores `key \u2192 owner.id` for future replays.\n24. **[S] Audit log** \u2014 writes an `AUDIT` info line with id, customer code, registration date, and computed `membershipLevel`/`membershipNumber`.\n25. **[S] Build response DTO** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto` derives read-only fields (displayName, salutation, initials, membershipNumber/level/points, fiscalYear, locality, timezone, contactPreference, telephoneDisplay, identityKey, checkDigit, ageBand, selfLink). These shape the response only; they aren't persisted.\n26. **[S] `Location` header** set to `/api/owners/{id}` and the response returned as `201 CREATED`.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging: the idempotency replay (step 3) runs **before** the required-field guard, and the future-date check (step 10) uses the date as submitted while all downstream date logic uses the business-day-adjusted date (step 12)."
